<Base title="Privacy & Local Data | Quilt Studio" description="Learn how the Quilt Studio calculator stores projects locally and what its code does with your cutting dimensions.">
<div class="page-shell"><div class="page-heading"><span class="eyebrow-with-line">— PRIVACY AT THE CUTTING TABLE</span><h1>Your project stays yours.</h1><p>Quilt Studio calculations run on your device. You do not need an account, a paid subscription or a cloud project database to use the tools.</p></div>
<section class="content-block"><div class="story-grid">
<article class="story-panel"><h2>Local project storage</h2><p>When you change project inputs, the tool may store a versioned JSON project in your browser's localStorage, so dimensions can carry between calculators. You can reset the sample, clear your browser data or save a JSON file yourself.</p></article>
<article class="story-panel"><h2>Import and export</h2><p>The file import control reads your selected JSON file inside your browser. The save and cut-plan buttons create files on your device; no project file is sent to a Quilt Studio account or server.</p></article>
<article class="story-panel"><h2>Hosting and future services</h2><p>Normal requests to load website pages and images may be recorded by the hosting provider. The initial code has no advertising or analytics integrations. If either is enabled later, this statement and applicable consent controls must be reviewed first.</p></article>
</div></section><p class="footer-note">Current code policy last reviewed November 2026. Publication and search indexing are separately checked during the production-domain release; this privacy statement describes the current browser-only software. See the <a href="https://github.com/garrison2025/Quilt_Calculator">source repository</a> for implementation details.</p></div>
</Base>
